menu "vterm"

    config VTERM_SCROLLBACK_LINES
        int "Terminal scrollback lines"
        default 1000
        range 0 4000
        help
            Rows of output kept after they scroll off the top, reachable
            with Shift+PageUp / Shift+PageDown.

            Costs lines * columns * 8 bytes, allocated once at startup and
            preferentially in PSRAM: 1000 lines at 100 columns is 800 KB of
            the ~8.3 MB free there, and none of the internal DRAM the render
            ISR competes for. A request that will not fit is halved until it
            does, so an over-large value shortens history rather than
            failing to boot.

            0 disables scrollback and allocates nothing.

    config VTERM_BENCH
        bool "Enable performance instrumentation"
        default n
        help
            Accumulates cycle counts and byte statistics across flush calls.
            Call vterm_bench_report() to log a summary.
            Zero overhead when disabled.

endmenu
